From fcaa25135534a627eaab8db857996a9b67109d76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fast llama project <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:10:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "vulkan: small batches use the decode-path activation
 precision rule"

Iteration 4 made Gemma's batched verification numerically near-identical to single-token
decode (mean KLD vs ub=1: 2.1e-3 -> 2.6e-5 at ub=5) but the float Q8_0 multi-column mat-vec
path is 14-25% slower end-to-end for MTP speculation (sessions it04-explore, it05-explore),
and an iteration-5 decode-once rewrite of that path did not recover the speed. Under the
Amendment 1 envelope, Gemma n=3 with stock numerics is admissible, so revert for speed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp | 9 ++++-----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
index 56a87a8..11d734f 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
@@ -6556,11 +6556,10 @@ static bool ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq(const vk_device& device, uint32_t m, uint32_
         return false;
     }
 
-    // Small batches (n = 2..mul_mat_vec_max_cols, e.g. speculative verification) use the same
-    // activation-precision choice as single-token decode, so that verifying drafted tokens
-    // reproduces the numerics of generating them one by one (fastllama iteration 4). The previous
-    // "always MMVQ for n > 1" rule quantized activations to q8_1 only in the batched path.
-    GGML_UNUSED(n);
+    // MMVQ is generally good for batches
+    if (n > 1) {
+        return true;
+    }
 
     // Quantization overhead is not worth it for small k
     switch (device->vendor_id) {
-- 
